# ==============================================================================
# Local Development / CI Secrets — root .env
# ==============================================================================
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values:  cp .env.example .env
# `.env` is gitignored; this example file is the tracked template.
#
# Loader: modules/shared/src/utility_envfile_parser.py (parse_env_file)
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub personal access token — required to clone PRIVATE submodules in CI
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The `verify` job in .github/workflows/ci.yml checks out submodules recursively.
# `internal/qwen-web-arwaky` is a PRIVATE repo, so the default GITHUB_TOKEN
# (which cannot read other private repos) fails with "Repository not found".
#
# Two ways to feed the token to the job:
#   1. Store this value as a GitHub Actions secret named `ARWAKY_SUBMODULE_TOKEN`
#      (Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions). ci.yml reads it via
#      `${{ secrets.ARWAKY_SUBMODULE_TOKEN || github.token }}`, so the job
#      still succeeds for public-only submodule sets without the secret.
#   2. Keep the same value in a local `.env` for `git submodule update --init`
#      on a machine that is not authenticated with the gh CLI.
#
# Fine-grained token minimal scopes: Contents: Read on rakaarwaky.
# Classic token scope: `repo`.
GITHUB_TOKEN="ghp_xxx_replace_me"
